The original reads the `type` and `profile` members more than once. This version loads each into a local once and adds a branch hint for the case where `type` is already set. Behavior is identical. The speedup will be small and is not measured.

```cpp
FIT_UINT8 Field::GetType() const
{
    const FIT_UINT8 t = type;
    if (__builtin_expect(t != FIT_UINT8_INVALID, 1))
        return t;

    const auto* const p = profile;
    if ((p == NULL) || (profileIndex >= p->numFields))
        return FIT_UINT8_INVALID;

    return p->fields[profileIndex].type;
}
```